[HEADING=1]AlmaLinux 10 + CentMinMod vs Ubuntu 26.04 + Angie — XenForo 2.3.13[/HEADING]

[B]Same 12-thread EPYC host, same XenForo dataset, PHP 8.2–8.5. CentMinMod left completely untuned.[/B]

[HEADING=2]TL;DR[/HEADING]

[TABLE]
[TR][TH]Metric (PHP 8.2–8.5 average)[/TH][TH]CentMinMod[/TH][TH]Ubuntu + Angie[/TH][TH]Delta[/TH][/TR]
[TR][TD]Guest cached page[/TD][TD][B]157,957[/B][/TD][TD]138,332[/TD][TD][B]+14.2 %[/B][/TD][/TR]
[TR][TD]Guest cache bypass[/TD][TD]596[/TD][TD][B]783[/B][/TD][TD]−23.9 %[/TD][/TR]
[TR][TD]Member home[/TD][TD]530[/TD][TD][B]691[/B][/TD][TD]−23.3 %[/TD][/TR]
[TR][TD]Member thread[/TD][TD][B]705[/B][/TD][TD]550[/TD][TD][B]+28.2 %[/B][/TD][/TR]
[TR][TD]Anubis cached page[/TD][TD][B]59,958[/B][/TD][TD]7,899[/TD][TD][B]+659 %[/B][/TD][/TR]
[TR][TD]Dynamic average[/TD][TD]605[/TD][TD]616[/TD][TD]−1.8 %[/TD][/TR]
[/TABLE]

[B]CentMinMod wins cached guest throughput and is dramatically leaner with Anubis. Ubuntu wins guest-bypass and member-home. Member-thread flips to CentMinMod.[/B] Overall, for a guest-heavy forum, CentMinMod Stack 3 is the fastest result in this comparison.

[HEADING=2]Environment[/HEADING]

[TABLE]
[TR][TH]Spec[/TH][TH]AlmaLinux 10.2 + CentMinMod[/TH][TH]Ubuntu 26.04 + Angie[/TH][/TR]
[TR][TD]CPU / RAM[/TD][TD]AMD EPYC 4245P, 6C/12T, 30 GiB[/TD][TD]Same host[/TD][/TR]
[TR][TD]Disk / OS[/TD][TD]2× 894 GB NVMe, AlmaLinux 10.2, kernel 6.12[/TD][TD]Ubuntu 26.04.1, kernel 7.0[/TD][/TR]
[TR][TD]Web server[/TD][TD][B]Nginx 1.31.8[/B], 6 workers, 300k connections[/TD][TD]Angie 1.12.4, 12 workers, 32k connections[/TD][/TR]
[TR][TD]PHP[/TD][TD][B]8.2.35, 8.3.36, 8.4.27, 8.5.12[/B][/TD][TD]8.2.35–8.5.12 (plus 8.6 RC5)[/TD][/TR]
[TR][TD]PHP-FPM[/TD][TD][B]ondemand, 30 children[/B], TCP 127.0.0.1:9000[/TD][TD]static, 12 workers, Unix socket[/TD][/TR]
[TR][TD]OPcache[/TD][TD]On, [B]JIT disabled[/B][/TD][TD]512 MB, [B]JIT tracing 64 MB[/B][/TD][/TR]
[TR][TD]Database[/TD][TD][B]MariaDB 10.11.19[/B], 8 GB pool, 600 conns[/TD][TD]MariaDB 11.8.6, 1.7 GB pool, 200 conns[/TD][/TR]
[TR][TD]Cache[/TD][TD][B]Redis 8.6.8[/B] + phpredis[/TD][TD]Valkey 9.0.4 + Credis[/TD][/TR]
[TR][TD]XenForo[/TD][TD]2.3.13 + 5 add-ons[/TD][TD]2.3.13 + 5 add-ons[/TD][/TR]
[/TABLE]

CentMinMod’s generated Nginx, PHP-FPM, MariaDB and Redis configurations were [B]not optimized[/B]. Only the minimal [ICODE]fastcgi_cache[/ICODE] layer and Anubis were added. PHP 8.6 is omitted because CentMinMod’s EL10 branch supports PHP 8.0–8.5 only.

[HEADING=2]Dataset and method[/HEADING]

[LIST]
[*]20,001 users, 10,000 threads, 101,134 posts (Ubuntu run: 100,400 posts), 51 forum nodes; Hampel Seeder.
[*][ICODE]wrk -t4 -c100 -d10s[/ICODE], 2 s warm-up, loopback HTTPS.
[*]Guest cached: [ICODE]GET /[/ICODE] no cookies. Guest bypass: [ICODE]xf_session=bench-bypass[/ICODE]. Member home/thread: fresh login cookie per stack.
[*]Page cache cleared per PHP version; Redis DB 1 flushed when toggled; Angie/Nginx rate limits disabled.
[*]Stack 1 disables the three SV Redis add-ons; stacks 2–4 enable all five.
[/LIST]

