[HEADING=2]PHP version comparison[/HEADING]

[TABLE]
[TR][TH]PHP[/TH][TH]CentMinMod dynamic avg[/TH][TH]Ubuntu dynamic avg[/TH][TH]CM member home / thread[/TH][/TR]
[TR][TD]8.2[/TD][TD][B]608.0[/B][/TD][TD]614.8[/TD][TD]530 / 705[/TD][/TR]
[TR][TD]8.3[/TD][TD]607.1[/TD][TD]612.0[/TD][TD]532 / 705[/TD][/TR]
[TR][TD]8.4[/TD][TD]604.2[/TD][TD]618.7[/TD][TD]530 / 707[/TD][/TR]
[TR][TD]8.5[/TD][TD]601.7[/TD][TD][B]619.5[/B][/TD][TD]526 / 699[/TD][/TR]
[/TABLE]

On CentMinMod, [B]8.2 is marginally fastest[/B]; on Ubuntu, [B]8.5[/B]. All four versions are within ~1 % on CentMinMod and ~1.2 % on Ubuntu. There is no meaningful PHP-version speed upgrade here; choose for support, not throughput.

[HEADING=2]Conclusion[/HEADING]

[LIST]
[*][B]Fastest cached guest stack:[/B] CentMinMod Stack 3, [B]157,957 req/s[/B], +14.2 % over Ubuntu Stack 3.
[*][B]Best Anubis result:[/B] CentMinMod Stack 4, [B]59,958 req/s[/B] vs Ubuntu’s 7,899. The CentMinMod Anubis integration is a minimal Nginx terminator; the Ubuntu one used Angie with branding [ICODE]sub_filter[/ICODE] and a static shadow, so this is not a like-for-like Anubis comparison.
[*][B]Best plain dynamic/guest-bypass:[/B] Ubuntu Stack 1, 783/691 vs CentMinMod 596/530. Ubuntu’s tuned PHP-FPM/JIT/MariaDB profile is doing real work here.
[*][B]Member thread:[/B] CentMinMod is ~28 % faster, likely because its stock ondemand pool allows 30 workers versus Ubuntu’s 12 static workers.
[*][B]Valkey/Redis alone:[/B] no gain on either platform; page cache is the only order-of-magnitude win.
[/LIST]

[B]Overall:[/B] CentMinMod is the better [I]cached guest[/I] and [I]Anubis[/I] stack on this host. Ubuntu is better for [I]guest-bypass[/I] and [I]member-home[/I]. For a guest-heavy forum, CentMinMod Stack 3 wins; for logged-in home traffic, Ubuntu Stack 1 wins. CentMinMod’s stock configuration is not a drop-in performance upgrade over a tuned Ubuntu/Angie stack.

[HEADING=3]Caveats[/HEADING]

[LIST]
[*]CentMinMod was deliberately untuned: ondemand/30 PHP-FPM, 6 Nginx workers, JIT off. Ubuntu was tuned by [ICODE]setup.sh[/ICODE]: static workers, JIT on, larger MariaDB pool.
[*]PHP 8.6 RC5 was not tested on CentMinMod; EL10 officially supports up to 8.5.
[*]CentMinMod used Redis 8.6.8 + phpredis; Ubuntu used Valkey 9.0.4 + Credis. A PHP 8.5 phpredis-vs-Credis control on Ubuntu measured within 1–2 %.
[*]Anubis implementations differ (minimal Nginx terminator vs Angie terminator with [ICODE]sub_filter[/ICODE]/static shadow); the Anubis delta is indicative, not an apples-to-apples proxy benchmark.
[*]Single 10 s run per cell; cache-hit variance on CentMinMod Stack 3 was 146k–170k across PHP versions.
[/LIST]
